# Line endings.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows but every container runs Linux, and files
# that a Linux shell interprets must not arrive with CRLF: a Dockerfile RUN
# line or a shell script with \r fails in ways that read as nonsense
# ("bad interpreter", "command not found" with an invisible character). Git's
# autocrlf setting is per-machine, so pin the behaviour here instead of hoping
# every clone is configured the same way.

# Default: normalise to LF in the repo, let Git decide the working copy.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files consumed by a Linux shell or Docker - always LF, no exceptions.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile*     text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts keep CRLF.
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.ps1           text eol=crlf

# Binary: never touch.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.parquet       binary
*.whl           binary
